From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: add verified firmware diagnostics

Expose the firmware 1.9.2 NGPHY, copper AN and DPC counters, the live
DPC PCS state, and the current rate-adaptation state through PHY ethtool
statistics. Add debugfs controls for clearing all three counter groups
and changing DPC rate adaptation with readback and rollback.

For explicitly marked diagnostic PHYs, derive the DPC PCS encoding and
SerDes rate from phy-mode. Read and record the previous state, program
the firmware, read it back, and expose the requested, previous, final,
error, and verification values. A failed diagnostic PCS write is
reported but does not abort PHY initialization, so a diagnostic mistake
cannot make the board unreachable.

Keep every DBGCMD/WBUF/POLL/RBUF sequence under the existing IPC mutex
and transmit the exact byte length, including one-byte payloads. Limit
the counter-clear file and startup PCS write to a DT opt-in property;
the ordinary AS21 device behavior remains unchanged.

The firmware DBGCMD ABI, DPC PCS layout, rate-adaptation commands,
counter layout and counter-clear order were verified against vendor
commit 56e0e77adad ("BPI-R4PRO Initial Version"), authored by wei.zuo
<wei.zuo@radisys.com>, and OpenWrt PR 24569 commit 80f610ddf007
("mediatek: filogic: add AeonSemi AS21xxx support"), authored by Sean
McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>.

The DT opt-in policy, verified PCS integration, failure handling,
statistics layout, and debugfs controls are new work.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
